NickelTouchRemote
=================

Turn pages on a Kobo with touch-screen style Bluetooth remotes ("TikTok
rings" and similar), in Kobo's own reader and in Kobalt.

Files in this folder (KOBOeReader/.adds/touchremote):

  config.sample.ini  Settings reference. Copy to config.ini to change the
                     button actions or options.
  config.ini         Your settings (optional). Defaults match the WX02 ring:
                     lower button = next page, upper = previous page,
                     middle = swap the two (switch hands).
  devices            Bluetooth HID ids the mod has bound to the kernel's
                     generic HID driver. Written automatically.
  uninstall          Create this file (empty) and restart the reader to
                     remove the mod.
  dumplog            Create this file (empty), then connect the remote and
                     press its buttons for a minute. The system log is then
                     copied to KOBOeReader/.kobo/NickelTouchRemote_<date>.log
                     and the flag is removed.

Pair and connect the remote in Nickel's Bluetooth settings as usual. The mod
only handles the input side: it gives driverless Bluetooth HID devices to the
kernel's generic HID driver, reads the simulated finger movements, and sends
the arrow keys a Bluetooth keyboard would send.
